Deliberately empty.

Alembic owns this database's schema — all 118 revisions of it — and this app
must never create a table in the catalogue. Laravel's skeleton migrations
(users, cache, sessions, jobs) were removed for that reason: `.env` points
DB_DATABASE at `book_scraper`, so one `php artisan migrate` would have created
four tables Alembic does not know about, in production.

If PHP ever needs a table of its own, give it a separate database or schema
rather than a migration here.
